  <prompt>Migrate the Create Analysis wizard (CreateAnalysisWizardWidget) to create sprk_analysis through the BFF child-records route with only user-entered values and no applyFieldMappings, and move the analysis to communication mapping (email subject/body) into the BFF send path, fill-only so a user-typed subject or body wins. Rebase onto PR #1501 first; run /conflict-check for CommunicationService.cs (UAC-r2 PR #2110 also edits it).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, React 18 / Fluent UI v9 code pages, Dataverse. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The widget has no applyFieldMappings call (create ~:906 and email ~:965); sprk_analysis is created via the route; CommunicationService.SendAsync fills an empty subject/body from the analysis to communication mapping and never overwrites a user-typed one; mapped fields on the new Analysis appear on first load.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-16, FR-17. CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx calls applyFieldMappings(parent to sprk_analysis) at ~:906, creates via childWrites.createRecord at ~:925, and on Send Email calls applyFieldMappings(sprk_analysis to sprk_communication) at ~:965 to derive subject/description. The server send path is CommunicationService.SendAsync (~:1490). PR #1501 overlaps the widget; PR #2110 overlaps CommunicationService.cs.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx (applyFieldMappings ~:906 and ~:965 REMOVED; create ~:925; email follow-on ~:957-985)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/__tests__/CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.test.tsx (payload = user-entered values; email request carries only typed subject/body)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs (SendAsync ~:1490: fill-only subject/body from the sprk_analysis to sprk_communication mapping when the analysis id is supplied)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Communication/CommunicationServiceSendMappingTests.cs (empty subject filled; typed subject survives; no mapping profile = unchanged)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/FieldMapping/CreateTimeFieldMapping.cs (canonical engine (task 001); fill-only applier from task 002)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateMatterWizard/matterService.ts (reference migration (task 021))</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs (created by task 012; Analysis and Communication rows)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="027" status="complete">Report Card migrated and live-verified.</dependency>
      <dependency task="019" status="complete">W2 service and canonical engine are live.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this wizard only. One wizard per task, live-verified on dev before the next starts (spec FR-16). Do not edit another wizard's files or bffChildWriteAdapter.ts beyond what task 020 delivered; if the adapter needs a change, stop and escalate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the create payload. The wizard sends ONLY values the user entered or picked (plus the filing/regarding keys the route needs). It must not call applyFieldMappings, read a mapping profile or pre-fill mapped fields; mapping, owner, search-index and I-1 stamp are applied by the server (FR-02, FR-06, FR-09, FR-10).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Scope: the shared UI library. Edits stay in Spaarke.UI.Components (or the named package) and the wizard's code-page host; no copy of shared logic into the host.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Scope: any UI touched by this task. Fluent v9 tokens only, no hard-coded colors, dark mode must render correctly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: deployment. Deploy through the code-page-deploy skill (build with the host's own npm script, never a hand-edited web resource). Rollback is redeploying the previous bundle; no runtime flag is added (spec rollout decision).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §9">Scope: auth. The wizard sends no owner, owning-team or impersonation value; the BFF decides ownership from the caller (FR-09). The route stays authenticated (existing authenticatedFetch).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. Placement Justification in the PR (extends the existing send path); publish-size delta against a fresh master build; CVE check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Scope: server mapping at send. Any payload check stays in CallerWriteAuthorization (path A); the send route filter is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: shared files. Rebase on PR #1501 before editing the widget; run /conflict-check for CommunicationService.cs against PR #2110 and keep the send-path diff minimal (one fill-only step), recording the outcome in the notes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Create Analysis wizard; analysis to communication mapping at send; fill-only semantics</topic>
