  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-16 (and FR-16 and FR-17), the create-surface inventory in notes/design-review-2026-10-19.md, CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx, and the existing tests listed in relevant-files. Re-grep the line numbers cited here before editing (they are approximate).</step>
    <step order="1">Rebase on PR #1501 (widget) and run /conflict-check for CommunicationService.cs vs PR #2110; record both in the task notes before editing.</step>
    <step order="2">Inventory keys on the sprk_analysis payload (~:818-905); classify user-entered vs client default; move defaults to the Analysis row of the task-012 registry or drop; list in task notes.</step>
    <step order="3">Widget: delete the applyFieldMappings call and result handling at ~:906 and the email mapping block at ~:965-985 (mappedSubject/mappedBody) plus the import (~:112); create via childWrites.createRecord (~:925), passing mappingSource when the filed-under parent differs from the intended source.</step>
    <step order="4">Widget email follow-on: send the user-typed subject/body (or empty) and the analysis id to the send route; do not compute mapped text on the client.</step>
    <step order="5">Server: in CommunicationService.SendAsync, when the request carries an analysis id and subject or body is empty/whitespace, fill it from the sprk_analysis to sprk_communication mapping using the canonical fill-only engine; a user-typed value is never replaced; no profile or unreadable source = request unchanged (no error).</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: widget test (payload user-entered only; email request has no mapped text); CommunicationServiceSendMappingTests (empty subject filled, typed subject survives, empty body filled, typed body survives, no profile unchanged, denied source Read = unchanged).</step>
    <step order="7">Build the BFF and library; deploy the BFF (bff-deploy skill) and the host that embeds the widget (code-page-deploy; grep src/solutions for CreateAnalysisWizardWidget to find it); measure publish-size delta and run the CVE check; live check: analysis mapped fields on first load, user value kept, owner = team; Send Email with an empty subject gets the mapped subject, with a typed subject keeps it.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If PR #2110 changes SendAsync's request shape or ordering so the fill-only step cannot be added minimally, STOP and escalate to coordinate with UAC-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If PR #1501 is not merged and cannot be rebased onto cleanly, STOP and escalate before editing the widget.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>CommunicationService has send-path tests for dispatch and recipients, none for subject/body derivation from a mapping.</existing>
    <extension>Extending an existing communication test class would mix transport and mapping concerns; the FR-17 proof is a named fill-only test set.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it a user-typed subject could be overwritten by a mapping and nothing would catch it.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Analysis wizard renders"><steps><step>Open the Analysis wizard code page on dev from its launch command</step><step>Step through to the last step</step></steps><expected>All steps render with no console errors; Fluent v9 styling intact.</expected></test>
    <test name="Analysis create flow"><steps><step>Fill the required fields and click Finish</step></steps><expected>The record is created through POST /api/v1/child-records/{table}; the success state shows the new record; no direct Xrm.WebApi create call for the table.</expected></test>
    <test name="Mapped values visible on first load"><steps><step>Create the record under a parent that has an active field-mapping profile</step><step>Open the new record immediately (first load, no refresh or save)</step></steps><expected>Every field the active Mapping Profile maps from the parent is populated on the new record at first load; no client write filled them.</expected></test>
    <test name="User value preserved"><steps><step>Type a value into a field the profile also maps</step><step>Finish and open the record</step></steps><expected>The user's own value is stored; the mapped value did not overwrite it (fill-only, FR-02). A user-typed email subject survives send; an empty subject is filled from the mapping.</expected></test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark mode"><steps><step>Switch the host to dark mode (theme toggle or prefers-color-scheme)</step><step>Open the wizard and step through every step</step></steps><expected>No unreadable text, no hard-coded light backgrounds, focus rings visible.</expected></test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools><tool name="npm">Build/test the code page and shared library</tool><tool name="code-page-deploy">Deploy the wizard web resource to dev</tool><tool name="ui-test">Browser verification on dev</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Communication/CommunicationServiceSendMappingTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx has no applyFieldMappings call or import (grep).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Server test: a user-typed subject survives send; an empty subject is filled from the mapping (FR-17).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">sprk_analysis is created through the BFF route with only user-entered values (widget test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; BFF unit tests green; publish-size delta and CVE result recorded; conflict-check outcomes (PR #1501, #2110) recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with a user value and a mapped value for the same field, the user value is stored; a mapped field the user never touched is populated on first load of the new record; the wizard payload contains no key the user did not enter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Deployed to dev via code-page-deploy; live check recorded in the task notes (mapped fields present on first load, user values kept, owner = owning team per FR-09); rollback bundle noted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Widget jest and host build pass; no existing test outside the Analysis wizard and send path changes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-16, FR-17. PR #1501 overlaps the widget; PR #2110 overlaps CommunicationService.cs.</notes>

